    {
      "id": "claim_8ab8d43a09cc420db00c7b70ae4c7f9c",
      "statement": "The full manifest's persistence API is explicit and inert by default: export_manifest writes a manifest as indented JSON to <directory>/capabilities.json (defaulting to haap_dir()) and returns the path, and load_manifest reads it back raising HAAPError ('no manifest at ...') when absent; per the module contract, capabilities.json is the owner's local artifact for deciding what to publish, and the document actually served to other agents is always the live public_manifest result, never a reload of that file.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/capabilities.py#L139-L156",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:cbf305de810126de8ef237acf3291c18da0c8c817c7a3920b55fd9bb0688b408:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/capabilities.py#L9-L12",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8a06a8da97aab0d15492956c06145689653bb7f4c8755e9a56c21d3a24081dd5:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_8f7d197907ce4374b4e1a2768f04a705",
      "statement": "parse_manifest is the canonical validator for manifests received from another agent: it accepts JSON str, bytes or dict, rejects non-JSON input, non-object JSON, and any manifest whose agent.fingerprint is not a string, and — as explicit defense in depth — rejects any manifest containing private_key, public_key or signature at top level or inside agent with the error 'manifest contains forbidden field ...: not processed'.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/capabilities.py#L159-L179",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:714593eb7064b2c5fa77085dc7bb09538042598c073896cb96872b0189ebbe6d:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d7051d462ec948dfacecd0f3ed0ec779",
      "statement": "For registry registration the public manifest is signed beside the keys, never inside them: registry_client.build_registration returns (public_manifest with messaging_url set, the identity's base64 public key, and an Ed25519 signature over the manifest serialized deterministically with json.dumps sort_keys=True, compact separators, ensure_ascii=False), and register() performs the two-step flow — POST /register, then signing the returned challenge nonce as the endpoint proof for POST /register/complete — raising DiscoveryError on any rejection.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/registry_client.py#L52-L89",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a76da6f5a63f0a6a91cf404c177542ee74b6b1530b35dcc1d275c93dcb756b7d:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_7016ad14ba7345e49b2f2e9a827ede64",
      "statement": "The registry's no-keys design: RegistryStore.submit_registration validates the fingerprint format (^HF-[0-9a-f]{16}$), that the submitted public key's fingerprint equals the manifest's agent.fingerprint, that the manifest signature verifies with that key, and that the declared endpoint is http(s); it keeps the validated public key in the pending challenge state precisely because the manifest never carries keys, and complete_registration lists the entry only after the endpoint proof verifies against that key within the 60 s CHALLENGE_TTL_S window. Re-registering the same fingerprint updates the stored entry, and entries expire after ENTRY_TTL_S (24 h) without a heartbeat, pruned lazily on read.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/registry.py#L35-L37",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2d2f822f91acc270861d13fe60c7ab97fd67aba2906f02ed25a1176f7fbb6c98:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://haap/registry.py#L60-L127",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5fa0b58567c41260d54c58853820e7250ad3e5ed94fe60ef1786026b941c6fb5:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_3434232cd9a04fb69fb2b1bf17ad95d6",
      "statement": "Directory search indexes the stored manifests: /search matches the capability filter case-insensitively against the union of tools, skill names and agent.speciality, filters the q parameter against the full manifest JSON, and returns only entries still alive within the entry TTL; registry_client.search consumes the results list.",
