    {
      "id": "claim_1f91f2bf2ad447c7b759c4ae877e40a9",
      "statement": "Manifest bytes never travel inside signed envelopes in v1: the capabilities message type is allow-listed in envelope.MESSAGE_TYPES and advertised in every manifest's MESSAGE_TYPES_PUBLIC, but the HAAPServer router implements no _on_capabilities handler — handle_message dispatches to _on_<type> only for handlers that exist and answers unhandled types with an error envelope ('unhandled type') — so capability exchange happens over HTTP well-known GET, registry registration, and the friend_request capability summary.",
